From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix infinite loops at EOF where char is unsigned

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/equinor/resdata/commit/ce341a3666855c57839466d9daa876252b54c8c0]

fgetc() returns EOF (-1) as an int. Three loops store it in a plain
char and then test c == EOF; where char is unsigned (riscv64, aarch64)
c becomes 255, the test is always false (GCC: "comparison is always
false due to limited range of data type"), and the loop spins forever
once fgetc() keeps returning EOF:

- rd_kw_qskip(): any formatted file without a quote character, e.g.
  tests/rd_tests/test_rd_file.py::test_broken_file, which hangs the
  test suite at that test on riscv64;
- util_fskip_lines(): fixed upstream by the commit above;
- fscanf_grdecl_data(): a trailing "--" comment without a newline.

Upstream fixed the first as part of the rd::KW rewrite (d9eacc14e,
skip_space_until_quote()) and removed the third file in c05264026;
all three fixes are in 7.0.0b3 and in none of the 6.3.x releases.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 lib/resdata/rd_kw.cpp        | 2 +-
 lib/resdata/rd_kw_grdecl.cpp | 2 +-
 lib/util/util.cpp            | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/resdata/rd_kw.cpp b/lib/resdata/rd_kw.cpp
index 17e08f4e7..f3c2475d1 100644
